No.  I agree with you mostly.  For every change I like in spork there
are two more which sound insufferably tedium-inducing.  The armor
destruction would be an example.  Ecch.

> What I see as needed to make the end game more
> interesting is more of the Lethe patch / Quest /
> Fort Ludius / Sokoban / Planes type of stuff, adding
> actual new interesting material to the game, rather
> than spork's approach of just making early forms of
> tedium last lots longer.

Hear, hear.  This is where the interest is kept: new and varied
situations, environments, terrains.  I agree vanilla could use a few
tweaks with respect to the difficulty of late-game monsters (e.g.
dragons as someone mentioned above), but the scale of the balance
overhaul being undertaken by spork seems, to me, disproportionate and
excessive.



